@echo off
cd /d "C:\Users\SubratoBiswas\trinamix-conversion-workbench"
echo Cleaning any git locks...
del /f /q ".git\index.lock" 2>nul
del /f /q ".git\HEAD.lock" 2>nul
echo Dropping tracked bytecode...
git rm -r --cached --ignore-unmatch backend/app/__pycache__ backend/app/services/__pycache__ backend/app/parsers/__pycache__
echo Staging...
git add -A
echo Committing (no-op if clean)...
git commit -m "Wave V: implement two missing transform rule types + fix Inactive Date and Enable B2B. During post-deploy download verification, Supplier Address Inactive Date output showed the raw Inactive flag (No/Yes) instead of a date, and Supplier Site Enable B2B Messaging was uniformly blank. Root cause: CONDITIONAL_DATE and MAP_BOOLEAN were seeded as rules but never implemented in transformations/engine.py, so they fell through apply_rule to passthrough. (1) Implemented CONDITIONAL_DATE in the engine: parses condition 'COL op VAL', reads the referenced column from the row directly, emits today's date (FBDI %Y%m%d) when the condition holds and blank otherwise (SYSDATE/today/now tokens -> today; null/none -> blank). Fixes Inactive Date: Inactive=Yes -> today, else blank. (2) Implemented MAP_BOOLEAN in the engine (case-insensitive true/false value sets -> Y/N with configurable outputs + blank default) for future robustness. (3) Switched the Enable B2B Messaging seed row from MAP_BOOLEAN to the proven CASE_WHEN-reads-source-column pattern (if_column Enable For EDI: Yes->Y, No->N, blank->blank), matching Delivery Channel/Communication Method, so it derives correctly regardless of base value-landing. (4) Registered CONDITIONAL_DATE and MAP_BOOLEAN in RULE_TYPES. The seeder upgrades the existing Enable B2B learning in place (rule_type change triggers rule_config update) on reseed. Unit-tested all three rule types; backend py_compile clean; JSON valid."
echo Pushing...
git push origin main
echo.
echo ====== DONE - Press any key to close ======
pause
